---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '@/components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-05-06';
---

<Layout title="Terms of Service — TTP">
  <Navbar />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 pb-16 pt-32 text-zinc-700 dark:text-slate-200">
    <h1 class="mb-2 text-4xl font-bold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="mb-8 text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="mb-6">
      By installing or using TTP (Talk To Paste, "the app"), you agree to these terms.
      If you do not agree, do not install the app or stop using it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">1. The service</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      TTP is a desktop application that records audio from your microphone, sends it to a third-party transcription provider (Groq), and pastes the result into the focused window.
      The app runs on your computer; we do not host or process your audio on our infrastructure.
      Transcription quality, latency, and availability depend on Groq and on your internet connection.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">2. Free and Pro tiers</h2>
    <p class="mb-3">TTP is offered in two tiers:</p>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li><strong>Free</strong> — full transcription functionality with capped AI Polish, dictionary, and history limits.</li>
      <li><strong>Pro</strong> — a one-time purchase that unlocks unlimited use of those features and includes free updates for the lifetime of the product.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="mb-6">
      A 7-day Pro trial starts automatically on first launch so you can evaluate Pro features before purchasing.
      The trial is per-machine and cannot be reset by reinstalling.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">3. License</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      We grant you a non-exclusive, non-transferable license to install and use TTP on the number of machines covered by your purchase
      (Free tier: unlimited installs; Pro tier: per the activation count shown at checkout).
      You may not redistribute, resell, decompile, reverse-engineer, or remove any license-enforcement mechanisms in the app.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">4. Payment, refunds, and cancellation</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      All Pro purchases are processed by Lemon Squeezy. Pricing, taxes, and currency are shown on the checkout page.
      Pro is a one-time purchase; there is no recurring subscription. Refunds are handled per Lemon Squeezy's standard refund window — contact <a class="underline text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-inherit dark:hover:text-white" href="mailto:amirksmain@gmail.com">amirksmain@gmail.com</a> within 14 days of purchase if the product doesn't work for you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">5. Your responsibilities</h2>
    <ul class="mb-6 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6">
      <li>You are responsible for the content you record and transcribe. Do not record people without consent or in jurisdictions where it is illegal.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for safeguarding your Groq API key. TTP stores it in your OS keychain, but you must keep your account secure.</li>
      <li>You agree to comply with Groq's terms of service for any audio sent through the app.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">6. Disclaimers</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      TTP is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.
      Transcription is performed by Groq; we make no guarantee about accuracy, completeness, or fitness for any specific use.
      The app may stop working at any time if Groq, Lemon Squeezy, or any third party we depend on changes their terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">7. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      To the maximum extent permitted by law, TTP and its author are not liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages,
      or any loss of profits, data, or use, arising from or related to the app.
      Our total liability for any direct damages is limited to the amount you paid for the app in the 12 months preceding the claim.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">8. Termination</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      You may stop using the app and uninstall it at any time. If you breach these terms (e.g. by attempting to circumvent license enforcement),
      we may terminate your license without refund.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">9. Governing law</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      These terms are governed by the laws of France. Any dispute will be resolved in the competent courts of France, subject to mandatory consumer-protection laws of your country of residence.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mb-3 mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">10. Contact</h2>
    <p class="mb-6">
      Questions about these terms:
      <a class="underline text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-inherit dark:hover:text-white" href="mailto:amirksmain@gmail.com">amirksmain@gmail.com</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
